  "measurement": "Each event has a unique seq and send timestamp (Date.now() in this process, same host clock assumed). e2e = time this process receives the pub/sub UI push {type:alert,alertId} on alerting:ui:push minus the send time of the event that produced the alert (alertId -> eventId from alerting:alerts, eventId -> seq from alerting:events). alertStream = alerting:alerts stream-entry time (Redis server clock) minus send time. notification = Notification.createdAt (enqueue time in the engine) minus send time, read from the ui-channel {type:notification} push; null when no delivery worker is running. Send time is taken just before the HTTP batch is written, so it includes HTTP, XADD, parse worker, Postgres insert, engine and pub/sub. Latency covers events whose alert was observed; lost = events accepted (HTTP 202) with no alert observed after the drain (parse + engine backlog excluded). backlog.delivery = notifications still in the delivery queue plus the per-worker processing lists (retry zset excluded: scheduled future work); it is counted in backlogAtEnd and a delivery backlog above the threshold marks the window overloaded, but never in lost (it counts notifications, not events).",
